      "readme_excerpt": "# Auto Loan Collateral Misrepresentation Fraud Detection\n\nMachine learning project to detect fraudulent collateral misrepresentation in auto loan applications using synthetic data and multiple classification algorithms.\n\n## Project Overview\n\nThis project develops and evaluates machine learning models to identify potential fraud in auto loan applications where borrowers may misrepresent vehicle collateral features. The analysis compares five classification algorithms, performs hyperparameter tuning, and provides model interpretability through SHAP analysis.\n\n## Key Results\n\n- **Best Model**: XGBoost Classifier\n- **Test AUC**: 70.83%\n- **Fraud Detection Rate**: 72.2% (Recall)\n- **Optimal Threshold**: 0.458\n\n## Dataset\n\nSynthetic dataset of 100,000 auto loan records generated using the Faker library with realistic fraud patterns:\n- **Features**: 141 (after feature engineering and one-hot encoding)\n- **Target Variable**: Collateral misrepresentation (19% fraud rate)\n- **Key Features**: LTV ratio, vehicle age, make/model, financing amount, collateral options\n\n### Fraud Generation Rules\n- LTV ratio > 1.1: +20% fraud probability\n- Vehicle year ≤ 2020: +10% fraud probability\n- Luxury brand",
